<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF in deal on Polish army radios.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF in deal on Polish army radios.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomson-CSF Communications, a subsidiary of Thomson-CSF, and Poland's Radmor SA signed a contract on Thursday to provide several thousand tactical radios to the Polish armed forces, the two companies said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The two companies said the contract was worth about $50 million and deliveries would start in 1997.</p>
<p>In the first phase of the contract, they would furnish Poland's armed forces with portable manpack and vehicle-mounted versions of its PR4G radio, the two companies said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
